  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The diborane molecule has two types of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> bond :<br /><br />(i) <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msub></math> -It is a normal covalent bond.<br /><br />(ii) <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> - It is a three centred bond (bridging bond).<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/5_solu_ca.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 98px;\" />",
